{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1533083-same-symbol-different-realm-arcanum","id":1533083,"title":"Same Symbol, Different Realm/Arcanum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-24T11:57:21-07:00","id":1533083,"title":"Same Symbol, Different Realm/Arcanum","content":"<br /> So I was having fun with this while talking with my new player, whose character was connecting with the symbol of &quot;Mother&quot; in her Awakening as a Thyrsus. So I kinda just tangented off a super-quick description of what the symbol of &quot;Mother&quot; would encompass in each of the five Supernal Realms: <i>&quot;the Primal Wild symbol of Motherhood would be very bestial, embodied, instinctual, physical motherhood. As opposed to, like, the Stygian symbol which would be all about ancestry and ghosts and memories, or the Aetheric symbol of like the wise all-knowing Mother who holds the secrets of life, death, and culture itself, or the Pandemonic symbol of basically all your mommy issues, or the Arcadian symbol of generational destiny and inheritance and ancestry.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> SO!<br /> <br /> Let's put out symbols and try to reinterpret them from the point of view of each of the Five Realms! (bonus points if you do so as each of the 10 types of Supernal entity, or add in the 5 Dur-Abzu). I offer as the first symbol for this game . . . Food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T07:06:00-07:00","id":1533122,"title":"","content":"Food in the Aether ? Communion wine. The Eucharist. The Body of God. All digestion is COMBUSTION. Cosmic<i> LIGHT </i>springs from the searing heat of the kitchen, transits through your aliments, then in-between the atoms that make you and keeping you moving in the great PATTERN !<br /> <br /> Food in the Wilds ? Almost too easy. All is flesh, that means all can eat and be eaten. Further, all has a flavor. Essence, most of all. Maybe what we call smell and taste are just the way we process this - the ties between emotions, composition, and sustenance. And of course, knowing the way tissues can be grown, seasoned, made palatable or poisonous.<br /> <br /> Food in Stygia ? Well, what happens to food that isn't eaten ? It spoils. But that's just... you know, also eating ? The necrophages and the mold. What happens after ? What remains when all those who could eat you have had their fill ? The inorganic. The forlorn. The truly unwanted, the true remains. That's what necromancer works with.<br /> <br /> Food in Arcadia ? All in the recipe. They all have a story, and they can all go wrong. Found randomly, but also random catastrophes. And all foods have their seasons, their occasions. Don't eat the food of the Fae, or it becomes your forever now.<br /> <br /> Food for the Mastigos ? Well... how about... no food ? Too much food ? Excruciatingly spicy food ? Cruelly obtained food ? Food you crave ? Food you hate ? What about forcing someone else to change their mind about a food, molding their psyche with the force of habit and compulsion ? What about finding the best restaurant, and the paths of sympathies of those who stop there ? Food connects. Food shackles you to who you are. All diets and regimens are authoritarian regimes.<br /> <hr /> <br /> Whew, that was fun ! (Entities and Dur-Abzu can be added by someone else). I propose my own concept... Marriage ! <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-29T22:44:37-07:00","id":1533372,"title":"","content":"Marriage in the Aether is the flame of passion, allowing the couple to forge mandalas of ambition, purpose and vision into new forms. But like all crafts, great care must be employed to guarantee the new item is more than the sum of its parts.<br /> <br /> Arcadia remembers the tale of the marriage in a piece of amber. Its facets infinite while the marriage lasts, each significant moment revealing a new one, perfectly preserving the memory within. Even should tragedy occur and it final form be set, it might leave a jewel worth treasuring.<br /> <br /> Pandemonium sees it as an thread of red iron. It can become rusted as personalities mutually shape each other, it may also be shattered by someone saying the right words at the right time. But it can allow one to find support when lost or a lifeline when one drops into a pitfall.<br /> <br /> In the Primal Wild it resonates as a duet, the passions of two living being turned into a song, the shared rhythm of their heartbeats expressing all the sentiments that words fall short of capturing.<br /> <br /> Stygia manifests it as an heirloom, with each significant member of each family having made their own addition to it. The couple adds their own segment to it, using whatever materials and artistic style best represents them, making it into a symbol of a shared legacy.<br /> <br /> So lets keep the momentum, the symbol I propose is The Messenger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-01-2024, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}